1. Work performed: removed the dynamic `cudaMemcpy(D2H, 4)` from [`runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu#L368), added `device_tensor_scale_ptr()` in [`runtime/include/nemotron/device_nvfp4_matrix.h`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/device_nvfp4_matrix.h#L35), and added a device-scale GEMM overload in [`runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_gemm_runner.h`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/nvfp4_gemm_runner.h#L39) / [`runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp#L694). The runner now checks the selected cuBLASLt algo’s pointer-mode mask, allocates cached device `alpha`/`beta`, computes `alpha = act_scale * weight_scale` on device via the helper in [`runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu#L522), and expert/linear callers now pass device scale pointers in [`runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L806) and [`runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp`](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L523).

2. Whether `POINTER_MODE_DEVICE` worked or fallback was needed: runtime detection is implemented, but I only verified by compile. At runtime the code will use `CUBLASLT_POINTER_MODE_DEVICE` when the chosen heuristic reports `CUBLASLT_POINTER_MODE_MASK_DEVICE`; otherwise it falls back to host alpha.

3. Compile status: both requested builds succeeded.
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4`
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4`

4. Concerns: the per-pack D2H in `PackInto()` is gone, which was the main stall source. The remaining fallback path is not the deferred single batched layer-level D2H described in the plan; if the selected algo lacks device pointer-mode support, it still does synchronous host scale reads inside the runner. Runtime profiling would be needed to confirm your actual NVFP4 algo stays on the device-pointer path.
